From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:47:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: show the backlog in the MO6TWPC profiles

TYN-only: flicking down (the engine's backlog gesture) ran the PC script's
backlog flow - MesRev(DispInit), then MesRev(Main) every frame, with
SW_SYSSUBMENUNO 1 and SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA ramping to 256 - but nothing was ever
drawn, and the script waited for the exit flag behind an invisible screen.
Two causes:

  - InstMesRev only called BacklogMenuPtr->Show()/Hide() for
    InstructionSet::MO6TW (PS3); the PC instruction set is a different
    InstructionSet value, so the fade never started. Accept MO6TWPC too.
  - profiles/mo6tw-pc/hud/backlogmenu.lua used DrawType ExtrasScenes (copied
    from the PS3 profile). The PC scripts treat the backlog as a system menu
    submenu, like the PC save menu, and that layer is the one drawn while it is
    open; use DrawType SystemMenu.

Observed on MuMu (Android 15, mo6tw-pc-zhs): after the change a flick down
opens the BACKLOG screen with the date header, name tags and the lines read so
far, and a two-finger tap closes it and the game continues with the next line.
Entry spacing, the scrollbar and the highlight bar come from the x1.5 scaled PS3
profile and may still be a few pixels off the PC game.

diff --git a/profiles/mo6tw-pc/hud/backlogmenu.lua b/profiles/mo6tw-pc/hud/backlogmenu.lua
index d176372e3dd78cce4067195a2f79fff1775b288f..3ba709ea978c7b6fbc44ce6bd78f28bb277fdce8 100644
--- a/profiles/mo6tw-pc/hud/backlogmenu.lua
+++ b/profiles/mo6tw-pc/hud/backlogmenu.lua
@@ -3,7 +3,9 @@
 -- The PC sheets for these menus were repacked, so sprite bounds are not exact.
 root.BacklogMenu = {
     Type = BacklogMenuType.MO6TW,
-    DrawType = DrawComponentType.ExtrasScenes,
+    -- The PC scripts open the backlog through the CC style submenu variables (SW_SYSSUBMENUNO 1) inside the system menu
+    -- layer, not on the PS3 ExtrasScenes layer, which is never drawn while the backlog is open.
+    DrawType = DrawComponentType.SystemMenu,
 
     BacklogBackgroundSprite = "BacklogBackground",
 
diff --git a/src/vm/inst_dialogue.cpp b/src/vm/inst_dialogue.cpp
index d25e6917eb5f2e5a9f4e9fdf84d21c606b74097b..15afbc1cd521398bd45c6297f2841e8f90752527 100644
--- a/src/vm/inst_dialogue.cpp
+++ b/src/vm/inst_dialogue.cpp
@@ -810,7 +810,8 @@ VmInstruction(InstMesRev) {
   PopUint8(type);
   switch (type) {
     case 0:  // DispInit
-      if (Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TW)
+      if (Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TW ||
+          Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TWPC)
         UI::BacklogMenuPtr->Show();
       ImpLogSlow(LogLevel::Warning, LogChannel::VMStub,
                  "STUB instruction SetMesModeFormat(type: DispInit)\n");
@@ -820,7 +821,8 @@ VmInstruction(InstMesRev) {
                  "STUB instruction SetMesModeFormat(type: Main)\n");
       break;
     case 2:  // AllCls
-      if (Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TW)
+      if (Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TW ||
+          Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == InstructionSet::MO6TWPC)
         UI::BacklogMenuPtr->Hide();
       ImpLogSlow(LogLevel::Warning, LogChannel::VMStub,
                  "STUB instruction SetMesModeFormat(type: AllCls)\n");
